+## hc doc
+
+```text
+Named JSON documents a core keeps (doc get|set), here or on a machine
+
+Usage: hc doc [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
+
+Commands:
+  get   Print a document's value (null when never written) and its version
+  set   Write JSON (the argument, or what is piped in with -) as the document; null deletes it
+  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
+
+Options:
+      --json  JSON output even in a terminal
+  -h, --help  Print help
+```
+
+## hc doc get
+
+```text
+Print a document's value (null when never written) and its version
+
+Usage: hc doc get [OPTIONS] <NAME>
+
+Arguments:
+  <NAME>  
+
+Options:
+      --json     JSON output even in a terminal
+      --on <ON>  Another machine's core
+  -h, --help     Print help
+```
+
+## hc doc set
+
+```text
+Write JSON (the argument, or what is piped in with -) as the document; null deletes it
+
+Usage: hc doc set [OPTIONS] <NAME> <VALUE>
+
+Arguments:
+  <NAME>   
+  <VALUE>  The JSON value, or - to read it from what is piped in
+
+Options:
+      --json               JSON output even in a terminal
+      --on <ON>            Another machine's core
+      --version <VERSION>  Only if the document is still at this version (from doc get); default: whatever it is now
+  -h, --help               Print help
+```
+
 ## hc events
 
 ```text
@@ -534,6 +587,8 @@ Options:
       --json               JSON output even in a terminal
       --if <STATUS>        Only type if the status is exactly this [possible values: idle, working]
